From 9a36005c9d657cfc1d0dc8c7e07be479953a4377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:48:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: the audio output follows the display when the
 configured one has none

An HDMI output without a display plays to nothing, and with some drivers
(snd-hda with an NVIDIA GPU) cannot even be opened: the engine is left
without a sink and there is no sound at all. It happens when the TV of a
machine with two GPUs is moved from one to the other, and on a first
start, whose default is the first HDMI output of the list whatever it is
connected to.

The ALSA sink already reads the ELD of each HDMI output. It now records
whether the driver says that a display is there, that none is, or
nothing. When the configured output has none and exactly one other
output of the same driver has one, the engine uses that one:

- every time it loads its settings (CActiveAE::LoadSettings()), so that
  the formats it passes through and the sink it opens are those of the
  output in use on every path: a new stream, a reconfiguration, the
  retries after an error;
- where a device that does not exist is replaced by "the first device"
  (CActiveAESink::ValidateOuputDevice() and the fallback of OpenSink());
- where the player asks whether a format can be passed through
  (CActiveAE::SupportsRaw()).

The stored setting is never changed by this, and a change of ELD is a
device change, which loads the settings again: the configured output is
the one in use whenever it has a display. With no display anywhere, with
several, or with an output whose driver cannot tell, nothing changes.
